---
// Where the external heat on a motor comes from, and the wall that it goes into: a vehicle in flight with its heat
// sources, and a section through the wall (boundary layer, external insulation, case, internal insulation,
// propellant) with the temperature through it. Schematic.
const ink = 'var(--rd-ink)', muted = 'var(--rd-muted)', hot = 'var(--rd-hot)';
const cy = 78, r = 20, xN = 24, xB = 92, xE = 352; // vehicle axis, body radius, nose tip, nose/body joint, end of body
const nose = `M${xN},${cy} Q${(xN + xB) / 2},${cy - r - 2} ${xB},${cy - r} L${xB},${cy + r} Q${(xN + xB) / 2},${cy + r + 2} ${xN},${cy} Z`;
// the wall section: layer boundaries (x) and the temperature through it
const S = { y0: 192, y1: 274 };
const X = { bl: 22, tps: 92, cs: 146, ci: 162, ins: 222, end: 418 };
const Tline = `M${X.bl},202 C${X.bl + 40},203 ${X.tps - 20},210 ${X.tps},212 L${X.cs},252 L${X.ci},253 L${X.ins},258 L${X.end},258`;
---

<figure class="viz heat-sources">
  <p class="viz-title">Where the external heat comes from, and where it goes</p>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 440 306" role="img" aria-labelledby="hs-desc" style="max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <desc id="hs-desc">
      Top: a vehicle in flight. The nose has stagnation heating, the body has a boundary layer at close to the recovery
      temperature, the fin leading edges heat strongly, and the aft end gets radiation from the plume and hot gas that
      flows back at the base. The motor section carries a thin layer of external insulation. Bottom: a section through
      the wall, from the hot boundary layer through the external insulation, the case, the internal insulation and the
      propellant. The temperature falls steeply through the external insulation, so the case stays below its limit.
    </desc>
    <!-- vehicle -->
    <path d={nose} fill="var(--rd-panel2)" stroke={muted}></path>
    <rect x={xB} y={cy - r} width={xE - xB} height={2 * r} fill="var(--rd-panel2)" stroke={muted}></rect>
    <rect x="150" y={cy - r - 4} width={xE - 150} height="4" fill="var(--rd-propellant)" fill-opacity="0.9"></rect>
    <rect x="150" y={cy + r} width={xE - 150} height="4" fill="var(--rd-propellant)" fill-opacity="0.9"></rect>
    <path d={`M${xE - 44},${cy - r} L${xE},${cy - r - 22} L${xE},${cy - r} Z M${xE - 44},${cy + r} L${xE},${cy + r + 22} L${xE},${cy + r} Z`} fill="var(--rd-steel)" stroke={muted}></path>
    <path d={`M${xE},${cy - 10} L${xE + 16},${cy - 15} L${xE + 16},${cy + 15} L${xE},${cy + 10} Z`} fill="var(--rd-steel)"></path>
    <path d={`M${xE + 16},${cy - 14} Q${xE + 50},${cy - 12} ${xE + 80},${cy} Q${xE + 50},${cy + 12} ${xE + 16},${cy + 14} Z`} fill={hot} fill-opacity="0.45"></path>
    {[170, 210, 250, 290].map((x) => <path d={`M${x},${cy - r - 18} L${x},${cy - r - 7} M${x - 3},${cy - r - 11} L${x},${cy - r - 7} L${x + 3},${cy - r - 11}`} fill="none" stroke={hot} stroke-width="1.4"></path>)}
    <path d={`M${xE + 34},${cy + 18} Q${xE + 14},${cy + 30} ${xE - 2},${cy + 24}`} fill="none" stroke={hot} stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="3 2"></path>
    <!-- labels -->
    <line x1={xN + 2} x2="40" y1={cy - 2} y2="34" stroke={muted}></line>
    <text x="42" y="30" font-size="10.5" fill={ink}>nose: stagnation</text>
    <text x="160" y="22" font-size="10.5" fill={ink}>boundary layer near T<tspan dy="2" font-size="8">r</tspan></text>
    <line x1="200" x2="200" y1={cy + r + 6} y2="122" stroke={muted}></line>
    <text x="200" y="134" font-size="10.5" fill={ink} text-anchor="middle">external insulation on the motor</text>
    <line x1={xE - 8} x2={xE - 30} y1={cy + r + 18} y2="138" stroke={muted}></line>
    <text x={xE - 30} y="150" font-size="10.5" fill={ink} text-anchor="middle">fin leading edges</text>
    <text x="436" y="13" font-size="10.5" fill={ink} text-anchor="end">base: plume</text>
    <text x="436" y="27" font-size="10.5" fill={ink} text-anchor="end">radiation and</text>
    <text x="436" y="41" font-size="10.5" fill={ink} text-anchor="end">hot back-flow</text>
    <!-- wall section -->
    <text x="220" y="166" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill={ink} text-anchor="middle">A section through the wall of the motor</text>
    <rect x={X.bl} y={S.y0} width={X.tps - X.bl} height={S.y1 - S.y0} fill={hot} fill-opacity="0.12"></rect>
    <rect x={X.tps} y={S.y0} width={X.cs - X.tps} height={S.y1 - S.y0} fill="var(--rd-propellant)" fill-opacity="0.55"></rect>
    <rect x={X.cs} y={S.y0} width={X.ci - X.cs} height={S.y1 - S.y0} fill="var(--rd-blue)" fill-opacity="0.6"></rect>
    <rect x={X.ci} y={S.y0} width={X.ins - X.ci} height={S.y1 - S.y0} fill="var(--rd-insul)" fill-opacity="0.7"></rect>
    <rect x={X.ins} y={S.y0} width={X.end - X.ins} height={S.y1 - S.y0} fill="var(--rd-propellant)" fill-opacity="0.3"></rect>
    <line x1={X.bl} x2={X.end} y1="232" y2="232" stroke="var(--rd-accent)" stroke-dasharray="5 4"></line>
    <text x={X.end - 2} y="228" font-size="10" fill="var(--rd-accent)" text-anchor="end">limit of the case</text>
    <path d={Tline} fill="none" stroke={ink} stroke-width="2.2"></path>
    <text x={X.bl + 4} y="214" font-size="10" fill={ink}>T</text>
    {[
      [(X.bl + X.tps) / 2, 'boundary', 'layer'], [(X.tps + X.cs) / 2, 'external', 'insulation'],
      [(X.ci + X.ins) / 2, 'internal', 'insulation'], [(X.ins + X.end) / 2, 'propellant', ''],
    ].map(([x, t1, t2]) => (
      <g>
        <text x={x} y={S.y1 + 13} font-size="10" fill={muted} text-anchor="middle">{t1}</text>
        <text x={x} y={S.y1 + 26} font-size="10" fill={muted} text-anchor="middle">{t2}</text>
      </g>
    ))}
    <line x1={(X.cs + X.ci) / 2} x2={(X.cs + X.ci) / 2} y1={S.y0 - 2} y2={S.y0 - 6} stroke={muted}></line>
    <text x={(X.cs + X.ci) / 2} y={S.y0 - 8} font-size="10" fill={muted} text-anchor="middle">case</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    In flight the air that the boundary layer brings to rest heats up to near the recovery temperature, and the heat
    flows into the wall. A few millimetres of external insulation with a low conductivity take most of the temperature
    drop, so the case behind it stays below its limit for the flight. The internal insulation protects the case from the
    combustion gas on the other side. Schematic.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
